    <section class="py-16 bg-white">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-5 lg:px-8">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-ink mb-6">How psychodynamic therapy works</h2>
        <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-8">Sessions do not follow a set agenda; you are free to speak about whatever comes to mind. The psychologist notices recurring themes and emotional patterns, and makes sense of them together with you. If you are looking for more structured, short-term work, <a href="/en/services/cbt-therapy.html" class="text-primary hover:underline">CBT</a> may be the better fit.</p>
        <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
          <div class="bg-warm rounded-2xl p-6 border border-warm-tertiary">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm mb-2">The Unconscious at Work</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Feelings and conflicts we are unaware of can quietly steer our choices and relationships.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-warm rounded-2xl p-6 border border-warm-tertiary">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm mb-2">Early Relationships</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Attachment patterns learned in our first relationships shape how much closeness and distance we need today.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-warm rounded-2xl p-6 border border-warm-tertiary">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm mb-2">The Therapeutic Relationship</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Patterns from outside appear in the consulting room too — a unique opportunity to work with them safely.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-warm rounded-2xl p-6 border border-warm-tertiary">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm mb-2">Lasting Change</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">The aim is not only symptom relief but a lasting expansion of your capacity to understand yourself.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="py-16 bg-warm">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-5 lg:px-8">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-ink mb-6">Who is psychodynamic therapy suitable for?</h2>
        <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-6">If what troubles you is less a particular symptom than a pattern that keeps repeating, psychodynamic therapy may suit. "I keep ending up in the same place" is the most common starting point for this work. It comes to the fore in these situations.</p>
        <ul class="space-y-3 text-ink-muted">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-primary shrink-0 mt-2.5"></span>Repeating relationship patterns and closeness that ends the same way</li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-primary shrink-0 mt-2.5"></span>Low mood that has continued for a long time</li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-primary shrink-0 mt-2.5"></span>Questions of identity, belonging and "who am I"</li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-primary shrink-0 mt-2.5"></span>Where short-term work has been tried but did not hold</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="py-16 bg-white">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-5 lg:px-8">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-ink mb-6">How long does psychodynamic therapy take?</h2>
        <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">This approach runs longer than the others. Noticing and shifting a pattern takes time, and the length is measured in months. Sessions last 45 minutes and are usually weekly.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">No end date is set at the outset. We review where we are together at regular intervals, and the decision to close the work is also discussed rather than announced.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="py-16 bg-warm">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-5 lg:px-8">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-ink mb-6">Do I have to talk about my childhood?</h2>
        <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">No. Psychodynamic therapy looks at early relationships, but that does not mean every session is spent on childhood. Most of the time we start from the present; the past enters when it is needed to understand the present, and when you are ready.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">You decide what to share and when. That also sets the pace of the work.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
